{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Sender recognition, not pattern matching. These load after 10-wallets.json,",
    "so a precise template always gets first refusal.",
    "",
    "The match is '.' - any non-empty message. All these do is put a bank name",
    "on the draft and let the generic extractors pull out amount, direction,",
    "merchant and card digits. That is deliberate: bank wording changes often",
    "and a loose rule that reliably labels the sender beats a tight one that",
    "silently stops matching. The generic amount extractor also knows to skip",
    "the running balance, which a hand-written per-bank regex usually does not.",
    "",
    "When a bank's format turns out to be stable and worth pinning down, move",
    "it into 10-wallets.json with named groups and a higher confidence.",
    "",
    "Add a sender by appending its SMS short-code / alphanumeric id to the",
    "senders list. POST /admin/reload afterwards."
  ],
  "templates": [
    {
      "id": "pk-bank-hbl",
      "bank": "HBL",
      "senders": ["^HBL", "HBLBank", "HBL ?Bank"],
      "match": ".",
      "direction": "auto",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
      "id": "pk-bank-meezan",
      "bank": "Meezan Bank",
      "senders": ["Meezan"],
      "match": ".",
      "direction": "auto",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
